{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/945224-how-to-justify-the-purchase-of-powerstat-and-powers-in-universe","id":945224,"title":"How To Justify The Purchase Of Powerstat And Powers In-Universe?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-06T19:12:11-07:00","id":945224,"title":"How To Justify The Purchase Of Powerstat And Powers In-Universe?","content":"What it says on the title. I wanted to see what the consensus was, especially regarding Changeling, Beast and Geist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T21:06:11-07:00","id":945265,"title":"","content":"For all splats regular use of their magic, 'feeding' their fuel regularly, and acting in line with the typical purpose of the splat (hunting a lot for werewolves, helping ghosts move on for sin-eaters, investigating mysteries for mage, etc) would all be good justifications<br /> <br /> Vampire: Doing the things that grant blood beats, even if you aren't using the blood beat system<br /> <br /> Beast: feeding your satiety a lot, spending a lot of time in your lair or imposing lair traits<br /> <br /> Changeling: Don't really need to justify it, the wyrd is very unpredictable<br /> <br /> Mage: Having earned arcane xp<br /> <br /> Demon: Hijacking infrastructure, using your demonic form, risking cover<br /> <br /> Werewolf: Taking down powerful prey, finishing the siskur-dah, shapeshifting a lot, facing breaking points (especially while keeping to balanced harmony<br /> <br /> Geist, mummy and promethean I am not familiar with enough to comment on","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T21:12:21-07:00","id":945269,"title":"","content":"Demons also gain Primum for uncovering their Ciphers.<br /> <br /> Edit: Oops, already mentioned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 08-07-2016, 12:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T23:59:19-07:00","id":945326,"title":"","content":"Use.<br /> <br /> Bout the sum of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T04:15:29-07:00","id":945394,"title":"","content":"The player wants to spend the XP. Unless there is setting material that says otherwise (i.e. another clan's signature discipline) or unless I think of an interesting way for them to learn something (i.e. I have a mentor I want to introduce) or there are other ooc issues involved, there is no actual benefit to the game for making them jump through hoops.<br /> <br /> In character, powerstats generally improve through use. Changelings learn contracts by staring at the thing they are contracting with for a long time and having a psychadelic vision. Vampires naturally develop their disciplines over time. Werewolves have to talk to spirits for new gifts, but facets just because. I would probably require talking to spirits for new gifts to at least happen, even if only offscreen. Beasts naturally evolve atavisms based on the local Hive or by being in a brood with other things that have those atavisms, or because it really fits in-theme. Beasts learn Nightmare by exposing themselves to things that elicit those nightmare or people experiencing that fear, which may be themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T22:01:51-07:00","id":949117,"title":"","content":"Anime-style training montages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T13:56:50-07:00","id":950208,"title":"","content":"I play in a Beast campaign--my ST and I generally agree that it's a combination of developing a greater connection with the Horror, and manifestations of fight-or-flight. Example: I play a Fire Elemental. Over time, she's getting a lot more fire abilities--but I had her develop infestation (a la fireflies) as a combination of her running away from a scary vampire lady and another PC who'd she'd angered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10141-solaris","name":"Solaris","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10141_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T14:01:34-07:00","id":950210,"title":"","content":"Wyrd is a cross between story narrative and fate, so maybe you did something that tied gou more closely to a story archetype or built up a sense of destiny about you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T16:04:38-07:00","id":950287,"title":"","content":"For Geist, there's probably an argument to be made for acting in line with one's Threshold in some manner (either by experiencing or perpetrating relevant circumstances) and/or for acceding to <i>some</i> extent to one's Geist's desires, goals, and the like (possibly leaving it more inclined toward lending either guidance or a bit more direct power). This being in addition to playing mediator between the living and the dead, mind.<br /> Or put another way: doing things that resonate with the relationship between life, death, and what comes after, especially but not exclusively if they hit close to home.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T19:23:32-07:00","id":950860,"title":"","content":"Personally, I like the idea of PC's going out and 'attuning' themselves to the thing they are trying to learn. A Changeling learning contracts of Smoke might go commune with a stick of incense, a Sin Eater learning the phantasmal key might take a three day acid bender, a Vampire learning Resilience might try subjecting themselves to small amounts of damage, and so on.<br /> <br /> Obviously this isn't a perfect system, but I like for my players to at least put the effort to try in character. It makes so much more sense to me than someone who has never shown a proclivity for something suddenly having a superpower in it just because they had XP to burn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2283-andreamus","name":"andreamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}